1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:11,026
One real research task. GPT five point six Sol and DeepAgents. Follow the complete recorded sequence.

2
00:00:13,550 --> 00:00:22,758
The paper studies consumption smoothing in interwar Japan. How does household consumption respond to disposable income?

3
00:00:23,483 --> 00:00:32,643
Six pieces must agree: data, regression, fixed effects, controls, clustered standard errors, and the result file.

4
00:00:33,483 --> 00:00:42,571
The reference stays sealed. The agent must produce the coefficient, standard error, and p-value without seeing it.

5
00:00:43,283 --> 00:00:46,371
Now watch the agent work.

6
00:00:47,083 --> 00:00:51,275
First, inspect the monthly household panel.

7
00:00:51,983 --> 00:01:00,591
Python loads the Stata file, then checks shape, column names, quarters, and candidate household identifiers.

8
00:01:02,817 --> 00:01:10,129
Eighteen eighty rows, sixty-three columns, four quarters, and two hundred thirty-seven households.

9
00:01:11,317 --> 00:01:16,277
Next, check the environment and usable observations.

10
00:01:16,983 --> 00:01:24,991
The code checks Python packages, missing values in eleven variables, and observations per household.

11
00:01:27,217 --> 00:01:41,273
Linearmodels, statsmodels, and scipy are available. Pyreadstat is missing. All eleven variables are complete, averaging seven point nine three observations per household.

12
00:01:41,983 --> 00:01:47,231
Now compare regression implementations and their standard errors.

13
00:01:47,950 --> 00:01:56,486
The program adds household and month-year fixed effects, composition controls by quarter, and household-clustered errors.

14
00:01:58,917 --> 00:02:10,981
The coefficient stays near zero point three nine one eight six five. Four methods give different standard errors. The small-sample correction matters.

15
00:02:11,683 --> 00:02:15,995
The agent now investigates the variable labels.

16
00:02:16,717 --> 00:02:23,765
Stata metadata reveals the data label, value labels, variable labels, and notes.

17
00:02:25,983 --> 00:02:37,807
H I D means household ID. T F E is the year-month count. Quarter maps the survey periods, and disposable income is measured in yen.

18
00:02:38,517 --> 00:02:42,205
Now the harness enforces the budget.

19
00:02:42,917 --> 00:02:46,437
The model proposes one more check.

20
00:02:47,150 --> 00:02:52,230
It requests another Panel OLS fit with a group adjustment.

21
00:02:52,950 --> 00:03:02,614
But four interactive tool calls are already used. DeepAgents blocks this request and asks for the final complete program.

22
00:03:03,317 --> 00:03:07,701
The sixth model call prepares the final submission.

23
00:03:08,417 --> 00:03:18,609
The final program removes household means, solves the regression, applies the clustered covariance correction, and writes the required JSON file.

24
00:03:19,317 --> 00:03:23,485
An independent evaluator now takes over.

25
00:03:24,217 --> 00:03:28,025
It runs the submitted program separately.

26
00:03:28,750 --> 00:03:36,902
The program exits successfully and saves a valid prediction: coefficient, standard error, and p-value.

27
00:03:37,617 --> 00:03:45,169
The reference is revealed. The coefficient passes its one-percent relative-error tolerance.

28
00:03:45,883 --> 00:03:51,299
The standard error also passes the one-percent relative-error check.

29
00:03:52,017 --> 00:03:58,345
The p-value passes a separate absolute-error tolerance of zero point zero one.

30
00:03:59,050 --> 00:04:09,386
All three pass. The earlier dummy-variable standard error would fail. Within tolerance does not mean identical digits.

31
00:04:10,117 --> 00:04:21,245
Complete reproduction: six model calls, four tool calls, forty-six thousand four hundred ninety-six tokens, and about two minutes of recorded runtime.

32
00:04:22,117 --> 00:04:33,341
One question, an executable program, and independently checked evidence. The complete recorded sequence is preserved, with a slower presentation.
